course: dictionary
lesson: 6306
title: Old words, new meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have fallen out of everyday talk, but you still find them in old books, fairy tales and poems. Morrow is one of them. When you meet an old word, use the context to work out what it means, just as you would with any new word.
explain: «Shall we run away to-morrow morning, quite early?» The words morning and early are clues. They tell you that to-morrow here means the day after today.
explain: Old books sometimes spell it with a hyphen, «to-morrow», and we now write tomorrow as one word. The spelling has changed, but the meaning has not.
explain: Morrow also appears in old greetings like «Good morrow!», which is an old way of saying good morning, and in phrases like «on the morrow», which means the day after.
fact: Morrow is a noun, and it is old-fashioned. You will mostly meet it in old books, fairy tales and poems.
fact: «Morrow» means the next day, or tomorrow.
fact: «Good morrow!» is an old greeting that means «Good morning!»
fact: «On the morrow» means the day after, or the time just after an event.
fact: The Bible uses it in «take no thought for the morrow», which means do not worry about tomorrow.
exercise: The old book says, «Good morrow!» What does it mean? | Well done, you won | Good night, sleep well | *Good morning | Goodbye, see you never
exercise: «Take no thought for the morrow.» What does morrow mean in this line? | A dark, quiet night | The last day of the week | The sea | *The next day, tomorrow
exercise: «The town was quiet on the morrow of the storm.» What does on the morrow mean? | In the middle of the storm | *The day after the storm | Far away from the storm | The day before the storm
test: «Here to-day—in next week to-morrow!» In this line, to-morrow points to a time that is? | *A time in the future, after today | Quiet and still | The very end of the story | A day that has already passed
test: Which word is old-fashioned and means tomorrow? | yesterday | evening | morning | *morrow
exam: Priya reads «The morrow brought bright sunshine after the storm.» What does morrow mean? | The middle of the storm | A grey cloud | *The next day, after the storm | The day before the storm
